    "static_alternative": "The sentence 'Nora walks to school every day' changes step by step into 'Nora is not walking to school right now'. First the -s ending lights up, because it belongs to the present simple. Then the time expression changes from 'every day' to 'right now'. Next the auxiliary 'is' slides in between the subject and the verb. The verb then loses its -s and takes -ing: from now on the person is carried by the auxiliary. Finally 'not' is placed after that auxiliary, because English makes a sentence negative on the auxiliary."
